    "note": "candidate-003 — fixed the value-disappears bug. Note this candidate has valueColor:\"\" (empty, the exact state that blanked your value) and the value renders fine now. Cause: `props.valueColor ?? theme.title` — an empty string isn't nullish, so a cleared picker passed \"\" straight through as the font color → invisible value. Fix: a shared resolveColor() helper treats empty / \"none\" / blank as 'use the default'. Since this was the same latent bug in EVERY Alpine color knob, I hardened the whole pack in one shared helper: kpi valueColor, line-chart lineColor, bar-graph barColor, donut segment colors all now fall back when cleared instead of vanishing. All 46 alpine tests still green; default colors unchanged (so the locked previews/masters stay valid).\n\nVALUE-COLOR INTENT: resolved — you meant the sparkline color (now direction-matched), and you confirmed the value color as-is (neutral dark) is fine. So no value-color default change; it stays a settable knob that now fails safe.\n\nSeparately filing your Make UX note: the message input is single-line and should grow with content (auto-resizing textarea) — tracked as a desktop-app task, not a template issue.",
